{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260614210814f9514247e4b0403a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see the current `defaultBuildSdkConfig` uses `defaultAssignments(model)`. For Story 6, I need to:\n\n1. Load assignments from config (using `loadAssignments`) instead of just using `defaultAssignments`\n2. Add startup validation after the instance is created\n\nThe challenge is that the config shape for assignments isn't defined yet. Looking at the story, the operator config should be something that can be passed through the ConnectorDeps or accessed from the ExtensionContext.\n\nFor now, since the story says \"Assignment quality is a dial-in concern, not a build gate\" and \"The epic ships with default assignments so derivations function\", I should:\n\n1. Add a config parameter to ConnectorDeps for assignment overrides\n2. Update defaultBuildSdkConfig to use loadAssignments with that config\n3. Add startup validation after instance creation in the session_start handler\n\nLet me implement this integration.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a10094db-b1fb-4175-b007-bb5af83ee62f","uuid":"c501b5d1-f32a-446d-bce5-05e18a42955f"}
