{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260614211023587e3a0e31b14b71","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see - ThreadRef is a union type where one variant has `filePath` and the other has `threadId`. In the tests, I'm using the `filePath` variant, which is valid. The TypeScript error is because it's not narrowing the type properly.\n\nLet me check the specific lines that are failing and fix them. The issue is that TypeScript doesn't know which variant of the union type we're using. I can either:\n1. Use type assertion\n2. Use a type guard\n3. Check which variant it is before accessing\n\nThe easiest fix is to use a type assertion or use the threadId variant instead. Let me fix the test file to handle this properly.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a10094db-b1fb-4175-b007-bb5af83ee62f","uuid":"bc4420d3-4453-4175-823b-3bc9db359cc6"}
