{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202606142111027b22d90151234e40","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the test, the issue is that I only set 2 kinds to use \"unknown\" provider/model, but the test expects all 7 to be unreachable. This is because the other 5 kinds are using the default \"pi-lhc/unconfigured\" which might be found in the mock registry.\n\nLooking at the `createMockContext` function, when no models are available, it defaults to:\n```typescript\nconst models = availableModels.length > 0\n  ? availableModels\n  : [{ provider: \"pi-lhc\", id: \"unconfigured\" }];\n```\n\nSo the mock registry returns `{ provider: \"pi-lhc\", id: \"unconfigured\" }` as the only available model. This means when we call `ctx.modelRegistry.find(\"pi-lhc\", \"unconfigured\")`, it will find that model and the lane is considered \"reachable\" (even if auth isn't configured).\n\nLet me fix the test to either:\n1. Make all 7 kinds use unknown provider/model (which would be more correct for testing \"all unreachable\")\n2. Or adjust the expectation to match what actually happens\n\nOption 1 is better for testing the \"all unreachable\" case. Let me fix the test.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a10094db-b1fb-4175-b007-bb5af83ee62f","uuid":"34fd2600-1c38-4bd9-a30a-f5ca216ccdb7"}
