{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260614211318201c1a8037094745","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see the issue. The `captureConfig` function is returning an old-style `SdkConfig` with `provider` instead of `inference`. This is the old API before Story 5/6 changes.\n\nLooking at line 42:\n```typescript\nreturn { ok: true, value: { provider: createDeterministicProvider(), mode: \"background\" } };\n```\n\nThis should be updated to use the new `inference` config shape that was introduced in Story 5. Let me check what the new SdkConfig shape should be.\n\nFrom the LHC SDK, the new shape should be:\n```typescript\n{\n  inference: {\n    call: ModelCall,\n    assignments: Record<FormKind, ModelAssignment>\n  },\n  mode: \"background\"\n}\n```\n\nI need to update the `captureConfig` function to use this new shape. This is a pre-existing issue that my change exposed - the test was using the old config shape.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a10094db-b1fb-4175-b007-bb5af83ee62f","uuid":"985ff24a-c750-44c3-b3e3-47deed928c78"}
